    "scenesThatPass": [
      "DIDO: Bette! No...no surprises Bette!\nLADY MARY: Girls! Will you refrain from shrieking like the...bless-ed French!",
      "LADY MARY: We shall receive visitors for dinner. The two girls exchange a glance and whisper.\nELIZABETH: Visitors? Who ever bothers to visit us here?\nDIDO: Or leave... except the dead!\nLADY MARY: Once again, Dido?",
      "LADY ASHFORD: This will be most interesting!\nLADY MARY: She has never played in company!\nLADY ASHFORD: She is...most accomplished.\nLADY MANSFIELD: Hers was a most diligent governess.",
      "DIDO: Papaa has never taken a pupil, you realise?\nELIZABETH: Someone to keep you company while you take Papaa's dictation, Dido. Truth is, there have been more of your sex at Kenwood this week, than I'…",
      "DIDO: Papaa.\nELIZABETH: There you are! DIDO is frozen, says nothing. ELIZABETH stares from the doorway - why does DIDO look so strange?\nELIZABETH: We are requested. You - drawing room. I, relegated to the ladies' Palour!"
    ]
  },
